c3=A.a([A.x(h8,"Payment in Cantonese Mahjong uses a fixed Faan-to-money table. It does NOT double each Faan - the common table is: 3F=$8, 4F=$16, 5F=$24, 6F=$32, 7F=$48, 8F=$64, 9F=$96, 10F=$128 (limit).",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Common fixed table: 3F=$8, 4F=$16, 5F=$24, 6F=$32, 7F=$48, 8F=$64, 9F=$96, 10F=$128 (the cap). Payment rises steadily - NOT by doubling per Faan!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Who pays? (Half-fire / \u534a\u9283 system) If you win by discard: the DISCARDER pays the FULL amount. If you self-draw: each of the 3 opponents pays HALF the amount (so you collect 1.5x total).",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Example: 3-Faan = $8. By discard: discarder pays the FULL $8. By self-draw: each of 3 opponents pays HALF ($4), so you collect $4 \xd7 3 = $12 total. Self-draw collects from all 3 but at half rate each.",h9,h9)],n5)
b2=A.d(h9,1,h9,"Half-fire system: by discard, only the discarder pays - the FULL amount. The other two players pay nothing.",A.a(["All 3 opponents pay equally","Only the discarder pays the full amount","Discarder pays full, others pay half","The dealer pays"],n7),h9,"You win with 4 Faan by claiming a discard. Who pays?",h9,B.h)
c1=A.d(h9,2,h9,"Half-fire self-draw: each of 3 opponents pays HALF. 3F=$8, half=$4, so $4 \xd7 3 = $12 total.",A.a(["$8 (from one player)","$24 ($8 \xd7 3 full)","$12 ($4 \xd7 3 half)","$4 (from one player)"],n7),h9,"You win with 3 Faan by self-draw. How much do you collect total?",h9,B.h)
b9=A.d(h9,1,h9,"Fixed table: 3F=$8, 4F=$16, 5F=$24. Payment rises steadily, it does NOT double per Faan.",A.a(["$8 -> $32 (doubles twice)","$8 -> $24 (rises on the fixed table)","$8 -> $16 (adds $4)","No change"],n7),h9,"Going from 3 Faan to 5 Faan, how does payment change on the common table?",h9,B.h)
o0=A.d(A.a(["24","$24","twenty-four","twenty four"],n7),0,h9,"The table sets 5 Faan at 24, and on a discard the discarder pays that full amount.",B.k,h9,u.bu,h9,B.w)
