c3=A.a([A.x(h8,"The discard pile is your crystal ball! Every tile an opponent throws tells you something about their hand.",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"If someone discards {{m1}}{{m9}} early, they probably don't want Characters terminals. If they keep discarding all suits EXCEPT Bamboo, they might be building a Bamboo flush!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Key principle: Early discards of a suit suggest they DON'T need that suit. Late discards of honors suggest they're not collecting them.",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Watch for patterns! If someone suddenly stops discarding a suit they were throwing before, they might have picked up useful tiles in that suit.",h9,h9)],n5)
c5=A.d(h9,1,h9,"Discarding multiple Circles early strongly suggests they don't need that suit.",A.a(["They're building Circles","They probably don't need Circles",l6,"Nothing useful"],n7),h9,"An opponent discards {{p2}}{{p5}}{{p8}} in their first 3 turns. What can you infer?",h9,B.h)
