b9=A.d(h9,0,h9,"Early discards are most informative because players discard tiles they definitely don't need first.",A.a(["First 3 turns","Middle of the game","Last 3 turns","All equally informative"],n7),h9,"When is a discard MOST informative?",h9,B.h)
c8=A.a(["They are unlikely to be collecting honour tiles","{{east}} is safe to discard against them for the rest of this rotation","They are definitely building a single-suit flush","They no longer hold any honour tiles"],n7)
c8=A.aS(c3,"8-1",A.a([c5,c6,b9,A.d(h9,0,A.a([0,1],p),"An early honour discard says little about suit shape, but it does mean they cannot use that honour against you this rotation.",c8,h9,"An opponent discards {{east}} on their first turn. Which conclusions are reasonable?",h9,B.B),A.d(A.a(["circles","circle","dots","dot","pins","pin"],n7),0,h9,"Throwing Bamboo at every rank early says Bamboo is not their suit, so the suit they never touch is the likely target.",B.k,h9,"An opponent throws {{s1}}, {{s5}} and {{s9}} in their first three turns but keeps every Dot tile. Which suit are they most likely collecting?",h9,B.w),A.d(h9,0,h9,"Early discards reveal what a hand does not want, while a sudden change of pattern reveals what it has started to collect.",B.k,B.WX,"Match each discard pattern to the most likely reading.",h9,B.C),A.d(h9,0,h9,"A middle tile is the most useful tile in its suit, so throwing it early is the clearest sign the suit is unwanted.",A.a(["s5","east","p1","m9"],n7),h9,"Four early discards from the same opponent are shown. Which one is the strongest evidence that they are avoiding the middle of that suit?",h9,B.F),A.d(h9,0,h9,"A late honour discard usually means the honour plan was dropped once the hand took its real shape.",A.a([u.P,u.o,"They have no hand at all","Their hand is already complete"],n7),h9,u._,h9,B.h)],o),l5,"What opponents' discards reveal","Reading Discards")
b9=A.a([A.x(h8,'A "safe tile" is one unlikely to help opponents win. The safest tiles are ones already discarded by the player you\'re worried about - BUT only within the SAME turn-rotation!',h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Why? If they threw {{east}} this rotation, they can't need {{east}} for a Pong right now. That tile is absolutely safe against them - until they draw again!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Once an opponent draws a new tile, their previous discard is no longer guaranteed safe. It becomes only RELATIVELY safe - they might have picked up a tile that now pairs with it. Re-assess every rotation!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Other safe tiles: tiles that multiple opponents have discarded, tiles where all 4 copies are visible, and tiles adjacent to their discards. Dangerous tiles: fresh tiles (never seen before), middle tiles (4,5,6) in late game.",h9,h9)],n5)
c6=A.d(h9,0,h9,"Within the same rotation (before they draw again), a tile they discarded is absolutely safe - they cannot need it for a Pong or Win.",A.a(["Absolutely safe (this rotation)","Relatively safe only","Dangerous","Unknown"],n7),h9,"An opponent discarded {{m5}} earlier this rotation. How safe is {{m5}} against them right now?",h9,B.h)
c5=A.d(h9,1,h9,"Once the opponent has drawn again, their old discard is no longer guaranteed safe - it becomes only relatively safe. Their hand may have changed.",A.a(["Still absolutely safe","Only relatively safe","Completely dangerous","Cannot be discarded"],n7),h9,"An opponent discarded {{m5}} two turns ago, and has since drawn twice. How safe is {{m5}} now?",h9,B.h)
